": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18593, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VfKErRcU1jXp7aR6tp9M67", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23544, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EM1Fbf9FfPGc2vcTUdYfKP", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 18%, all regions: us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. First rollback attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 (mixed state). A second rollback attempt completed successfully. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: (1) investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure before re-deploying; (2) investigate the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback mid-rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54144, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EM1Fbf9FfPGc2vcTUdYfKP", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54144, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EM1Fbf9FfPGc2vcTUdYfKP", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55782, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01ShDPscJeL1ze3XkBHSSudz", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56082, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ShDPscJeL1ze3XkBHSSudz", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56082, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ShDPscJeL1ze3XkBHSSudz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62870, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The incident was created despite the timeout (INC-0001), so no retry was needed.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Rollback completed** \u2014 checkout-api is now on **v2.3.0** in all regions and healthy.\n\n- **Diagnosis:** v2.3.1 was deployed to us-east, us-west, and eu-west and was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent production-healthy release (v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy, so not a valid target).\n- **Rollback:** The first rollback attempt partially failed \u2014 the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving the service in a mixed state (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west still on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback and it completed successfully across all three regions.\n- **Verification:** Service is now `healthy: true` with error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api. The create call timed out, but I confirmed via `list_incidents` that it was created, so I didn't retry (avoiding a duplicate page). The summary documents the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state, and two follow-ups: root-causing v2.3.1 and investigating the orchestrator error.\n\nOne thing worth flagging to the team: the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback mid-rollout is a separate reliability concern \u2014 a rollback that strands regions in a mixed state is dangerous during an incident, and I've noted it in the incident for follow-up.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the current status and release history for checkout-api.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BPZZ99JsLPJqb3hrCCeyt7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01F9YkJyqB4HivKiSiLVihtY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013w4sydxnkncguYnU8xzaBE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback halted after us-east. Let me check the current state before deciding next steps.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WwYkThDz8LgA8x4rRgC6sn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The service is now in a mixed state: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on the broken v2.3.1. I'll retry the rollback to complete the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0192L5tJzckJ5qxsFbwGq432", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The retry succeeded \u2014 all three regions are now on v2.3.0. Let me verify health and open the incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VfKErRcU1jXp7aR6tp9M67", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EM1Fbf9FfPGc2vcTUdYfKP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 18%, all regions: us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. First rollback attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1 (mixed state). A second rollback attempt completed successfully. Current state: all three regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: (1) investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure before re-deploying; (2) investigate the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback mid-rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident creation timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was actually created to avoid paging on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ShDPscJeL1ze3XkBHSSudz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The incident was created despite the timeout (INC-0001), so no retry was needed.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Rollback completed** \u2014 checkout-api is now on **v2.3.0** in all regions and healthy.\n\n- **Diagnosis:** v2.3.1 was deployed to us-east, us-west, and eu-west and was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent production-healthy release (v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy, so not a valid target).\n- **Rollback:** The first rollback attempt partially failed \u2014 the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving the service in a mixed state (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west still on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback and it completed successfully across all three regions.\n- **Verification:** Service is now `healthy: true` with error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api. The create call timed out, but I confirmed via `list_incidents` that it was created, so I didn't retry (avoiding a duplicate page). The summary documents the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current state, and two follow-ups: root-causing v2.3.1 and investigating the orchestrator error.\n\nOne thing worth flagging to the team: the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback mid-rollout is a separate reliability concern \u2014 a rollback that strands regions in a mixed state is dangerous during an incident, and I've noted it in the incident for follow-up.", "type": "text"}]}]}